//! Error: an `extern(ffi, "lib")` wrapper's return representation is decided
//!        from the DECLARED Rock type -- the `ffi.cdef` lives in an opaque
//!        `inline(lua)` body, so the declaration is the only contract the
//!        compiler has. A generic parameter is not a contract: nothing about
//!        `T` says whether the C callee hands back a number, a BOXED 64-bit
//!        integer or a struct, so there is no representation to give it. An
//!        UNBOUND one, specifically: `-> Boxed<int>` binds `T` and compiles.
//!        Rejected at emit rather than emitting a passthrough wrapper, which is
//!        the same fail-open that let 64-bit handles cross the FFI boundary as
//!        cdata into a Rock `int`.
//!
//!        The concrete-return externs stay legal and are exercised by
//!        `tests/extern_fn_value.rock`; this rejects only the
//!        shape that has no representation to pick.
//! Tags: extern, ffi, generics, c-boundary, emit-time

//=== TEST CASE: extern_ffi_generic_return ===
extern(ffi, "m") fn opaque_ret<T>() -> T

fn main() {
    print("unreachable")
}
